hadiths[75]{hadithnumber,text}:
"110","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The prayer of a person who has had a hadath is not accepted until he performs ablution."" A man from Hadramaut (a city) asked, ""O Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)! What is 'hadath'?"" He replied, ""The passing of wind, whether with or without sound."""
"111","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""My Ummah will be called on the Day of Resurrection with their limbs shining due to the traces of ablution, such as their hands, feet, etc., shining because of ablution. So whoever among you can increase the brightness should do so."""
"112","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the condition of a person was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who imagines that he feels something (i.e., wind) passing during prayer. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said that he should not leave (the prayer) or turn away until he hears a sound or perceives a smell."
"113","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): One night I stayed at the house of my maternal aunt, Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her). When a part of the night had passed, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up and performed a light ablution from a hanging water-skin.... (Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, offered the Tahajjud prayer.... This hadith is mentioned in multiple chapters.)"
"114","Narrated Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed from ‘Arafah, and when he reached the valley, he dismounted and urinated, then performed ablution, but did not complete the ablution. So I said, “O Messenger of Allah! (The time for) prayer is near.” He (peace be upon him) said, “The prayer is ahead of you (i.e., we will pray in Muzdalifah).” When he reached Muzdalifah, he dismounted and performed complete ablution. Then the call for the establishment of prayer (iqamah) was given, and he (peace be upon him) led the Maghrib prayer. After that, everyone made their camels kneel at their places. Then the iqamah for the ‘Isha prayer was given, and he (peace be upon him) led the prayer, and he did not pray any (optional) prayer between the two."
"115","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he performed ablution, so he took a handful of water and with it rinsed his mouth and put water into his nose. Then he took a handful of water and did like this, meaning he rubbed both hands together and washed his face with that handful. Then he took a handful of water and washed his right hand, then took a handful of water and washed his left hand (up to the elbow). Then he took a handful of water and poured it over his right foot until he washed it, then took another handful of water and washed his left foot with it. Then (Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) perform ablution in this manner."
"116","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter the toilet, he would say, ""O Allah, I seek refuge with You from male and female evil jinn."""
"117","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that (on one occasion) when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the toilet, I placed water for his ablution. (When the Prophet came out from there) he asked: ""Who placed this water?"" He was informed, so he said: ""O Allah, grant him understanding of the religion."""
"118","Narrated Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When any one of you goes to the toilet, he should neither face the Qiblah nor turn his back towards it. Rather, he should face towards the east or the west. (In those countries where the Qiblah is towards the west, one should face north or south.)"
"119","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to say: People say that when you sit for relieving yourself, neither face the Qiblah nor face Bait-ul-Maqdis. But one day I climbed to the roof of my house and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting on two bricks for relieving himself, facing towards Bait-ul-Maqdis."
"120","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa Tayyiba Tahira (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the wives of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would go out at night for relieving themselves, they would go towards Manasi’ (which means a spacious mound). Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) that you should make your wives observe veiling, but the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not do so. Then one night at the time of Isha, Ummul Momineen Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her), that is, the wife of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), went out and she was a tall woman. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), out of the desire that the command of veiling be revealed, called out, “Be aware, O Sawda! We have recognized you.” So Allah the Exalted revealed the command of veiling."
"121","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to relieve himself, I and another boy (both) would go behind him, and we would have a water container (vessel) with us."
"122","(From Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, as well) — In another narration it is reported that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would go to relieve himself, I and another boy would carry a vessel of water and a small spear; the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would cleanse himself with the water."
"123","Narrated from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any of you drinks water, he should not breathe into the vessel, and when he goes to the toilet, he should not touch his private part with his right hand, nor should he clean himself with his right hand."
"124","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` I walked behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) while he had gone out to relieve himself, and it was his habit that he would not look here and there. So I came close to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Find me some stones so that I may purify myself with them."" (Or he said some words similar to this.) ""And do not bring me any bones or dung."" So I brought some stones in the edge of my garment and placed them beside the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and then I moved away from him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had finished relieving himself, he used the stones."
"125","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself and ordered me to bring him three stones. I found two stones and searched for a third but could not find it, so I brought a piece of dried dung and brought it to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: ""This is impure."""
"126","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution and washed each limb once."
"127","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and washed each limb twice."
"128","('Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Humran, the freed slave of Hazrat Uthman, informed that) Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) called for a vessel of water and poured water on his palms three times and washed them. (Then he took water in his hand) and rinsed his mouth and cleaned his nose. Then he washed his face three times and both hands up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head, then washed both his feet up to the ankles three times. Then he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine and then offers two units of prayer in which he does not talk to himself with his heart, all his past sins will be forgiven."""
"129","‘And in another hadith,’ Amir al-Mu’minin Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said (after performing ablution): I will tell you a hadith; if there were not a verse of the Qur’an, I would not have told you this hadith. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever performs ablution well and then offers prayer (any obligatory prayer), then the sins committed between that prayer and the next prayer will be forgiven.” (Urwah said): That verse (from Surah Al-Baqarah) is: “Indeed, those who conceal what We have sent down of clear proofs and guidance…” till the end."
"130","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution should clean his nose, and whoever uses stones for istinja should use an odd number (of stones)."""
"131","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you performs ablution, he should put water into his nose and then clean it, and whoever uses stones for istinja, he should do so with an odd number (of stones), and when any one of you wakes up from his sleep, he should wash his hand before putting it into the water for ablution, because none of you knows where his hand has been (on which parts of his body it has passed) during the night."""
"132","Ibn Huraij said to (Sayyiduna) Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): ""I have seen that (during Tawaf) you do not touch any corner except the two Yemeni corners, and I have seen that you wear Sabti sandals, and I have seen that you dye (your hair or clothes) with yellow color, and I have seen that when you are in Makkah, other people, as soon as they see the (crescent of Dhul-Hijjah), put on Ihram, but you do not put on Ihram until the day of Tarwiyah (the 8th of Dhul-Hijjah)."" So Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""Indeed, I do these things. As for touching the Yemeni corners during Tawaf, I have not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) touch any corner except these two Yemeni corners. As for the Sabti sandals, indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wearing such sandals that had no hair on them, and he would perform ablution in those sandals (i.e., he would wash his feet, not wipe over them). Therefore, I like to wear such sandals. As for the yellow color, indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) dyeing with it. Therefore, I like to dye with it. And as for putting on Ihram, I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) put on Ihram until his mount moved (i.e., on the eighth day)."""
"133","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to start with the right side in wearing shoes, combing his hair, performing purification (wudu, ghusl), and (in fact, in all matters)."
"134","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the time for prayer had come and people searched for water for ablution but could not find any. Then water for ablution was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a vessel. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand in that vessel and ordered the people: ""Perform ablution with this."" Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw water gushing forth from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until all the people had performed ablution."
"135","And Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) also narrates that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his head shaved, Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) was the first to take the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"136","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a dog drinks water or anything else from someone's vessel, he should wash it seven times."""
"137","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): During the time of Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him), dogs used to come and go in the mosque, and sometimes they would urinate there, but the people did not sprinkle water or anything (to clean) because of their coming and going."
"138","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A servant remains in the state of prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer in the mosque, unless he loses his ablution."""
"139","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Commander of the Faithful, Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Tell me, if (a person) has intercourse but there is no ejaculation, what is the ruling?"" So Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""He should perform ablution as he does for prayer and wash his private part."" Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) says, ""I heard this issue from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" (Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him), the narrator of the hadith, says that) then I asked this issue to Ali, Zubair, Talha, and Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them), and they (also) gave the same ruling to that person."
"140","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to an Ansari person (to call him), so he came while water (of bathing) was dripping from his head. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perhaps we hurried you (in calling you)?"" He replied, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When there is haste or (for some other reason) there is no ejaculation, then only ablution (wudu) is obligatory upon you (ghusl is not obligatory)."" (But this ruling is abrogated.)"
"141","Narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself. (When the Prophet returned,) Mughirah began to pour water for him (over his blessed limbs), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, that is, he washed his mouth and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his socks (as well)."
"142","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` he spent a night in the house of the Prophet Muhammad’s (peace and blessings be upon him) wife, Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) (and she was his maternal aunt). (Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says:) I lay down across the width of the bed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his wife Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) lay down along its length. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slept until, when half the night had passed, or a little before or after it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up and sat, wiping the traces of sleep from his blessed face with his hand. Then he recited the last ten verses of Surah Al-Imran. After that, he went to a hanging water-skin, performed ablution from it thoroughly, and then stood up to pray. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: I also got up and did as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had done. Then I stood on his left side, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his right hand on my head, took hold of my ear and twisted it, and made me stand on his right side. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed two rak‘ahs, then two rak‘ahs, then two rak‘ahs, then two rak‘ahs, then two rak‘ahs, then two rak‘ahs, then he prayed Witr. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down until the mu’adhdhin came to him, so he stood up and prayed two light (Sunnah of Fajr) rak‘ahs, then he went out and prayed the morning prayer."
"143","A person said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Can you show me how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution?"" Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Yes, I can show you."" Then he called for water and poured it on his hand, then washed his hands twice, then rinsed his mouth three times and put water into his nose and blew it out, then washed his face three times, then washed both his hands up to the elbows twice, then wiped his head with both his hands, that is, he brought them forward and then back. He started from the front part of the head and took both hands to the nape, then brought them back to where he had started. Then he washed both his feet."
"144","Narrated Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him): (One day) the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us at midday, and water for ablution was brought to him. So, he performed ablution. When he had finished ablution, the people began to take the leftover water from his ablution and started rubbing it on their faces and eyes. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) offered two rak‘ahs of Zuhr and two rak‘ahs of ‘Asr (shortened), and in front of him a spear (i.e., a lance) was fixed as a sutrah (barrier)."
"145","Saidna Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that my maternal aunt took me to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The son of my sister (this boy) is ill."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand on my head and prayed for blessings for me. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, and I drank the water that remained from his ablution. Then I stood behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and I saw the Seal of Prophethood, which was between his two shoulders and was like the knob of a canopy."
"146","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), men and women used to perform ablution together from the same vessel."
"147","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me when I was so ill that I could not understand anything. So he performed ablution and sprinkled the leftover water of his ablution over me, and I regained consciousness. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who will inherit from me? I have only one kalalah (distant relative) as an heir."" Then the verse of inheritance was revealed."
"148","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the time for prayer came, the person whose house was nearby went (to his house to perform ablution), and a few people remained. Then a stone vessel (container) was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in which there was water, and the vessel was not spacious enough for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to spread his palm in it. So all the people performed ablution (with that small amount of water). (The narrator Humayd says) We asked (Anas, may Allah be pleased with him), how many people were you (at that time)? He said, eighty or even more than eighty."
"149","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for a vessel (bowl) in which there was water, then he washed his both hands and blessed face in it, and rinsed his mouth in it as well."
"150","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) became heavy (with illness) in his final sickness and his illness became severe, he (peace be upon him) sought permission from his wives to be nursed in my (Aisha’s) house, so all of them gave him permission. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) came out (to go to my house) supported between two men, and his (blessed) feet were dragging on the ground as he walked. And the Prophet (peace be upon him) came out with Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) and another man (Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him), and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) had come to his house and his illness increased further, he (peace be upon him) said: “Pour seven water skins over me whose knots have not been untied, so that I may advise the people.” (So this was done.) And the Prophet (peace be upon him) was seated in the washbasin of Umm al-Mu’minin Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him). After that, we began to pour water over him (peace be upon him) until he (peace be upon him) gestured to us that (now you have fulfilled the command). After that, the Prophet (peace be upon him) went out to the people."
"151","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for a vessel of water, so a wide-mouthed, shallow bowl was brought before him in which there was some water. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his fingers into it. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was watching the water gushing forth from between the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a spring. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I estimated the people who performed ablution with that water, and they were between seventy and eighty."
"152","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wash his body or (he said) when he used to bathe, he would use from one sa’ to five mudd (of water), and for ablution he would use one mudd (of water)."
"153","‘The conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wiped over the leather socks (khuffs). And Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) asked (his father) Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) about this matter, so he said: Yes. When Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates any report to you from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then do not ask anyone else about it (for confirmation).’"
"154","Sayyiduna Amr bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over both his leather socks."
"155","Narrated by Sayyiduna Amr ibn Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him): I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wiping over his turban and both his leather socks."
"156","Narrated Sayyiduna Mughira (may Allah be pleased with him): I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, so when it was time for ablution, I intended to remove both of his leather socks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Leave them, for I put them on while my feet were in a state of purity."" Then he wiped over them."
"157","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Amr bin Umayyah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ate a shoulder of a goat, then he was called for prayer. So he, peace and blessings be upon him, put down the knife. After that, he, peace and blessings be upon him, performed the prayer and did not perform ablution (again)."
"158","Narrated from Sayyiduna Suwaid bin Nu'man (may Allah be pleased with him) that in the year of (the conquest of) Khaybar, he went along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when they reached (the place) Sahba, which was very close to Khaybar, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the 'Asr prayer and then asked for food (breakfast). The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) brought only sattu (barley flour) to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He ordered it to be mixed with water, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and all of us ate it. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to perform the Maghrib prayer and (only) rinsed his mouth, and we (also only) rinsed our mouths and performed the prayer, and did not perform ablution (again)."
"159","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) that (once) the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ate the meat of (a goat's) shoulder at her place, then offered prayer and did not perform ablution."
"160","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk, then rinsed his mouth and said: ""There is greasiness in milk."""
"161","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you becomes drowsy while praying, he should (break the prayer and) go to sleep until his sleep goes away. Because if any one of you prays in a state of sleepiness, he does not know (what he is saying); perhaps he intends to seek forgiveness but (unknowingly) he may curse himself."""
"162","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""When any one of you becomes drowsy during prayer, he should sleep until (his sleep goes away and) he understands what he is reciting."""
"163","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution for every prayer. (He further) says that for each of us, one ablution was sufficient unless he committed hadath (lost his state of purity)."
"164","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a garden from among the gardens of Madinah or Makkah and heard the voices of two men who were being punished in their graves. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are being punished, and (apparently) they are not being punished for a major matter."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes (the fact is that) one of them did not protect himself from urine (splashes), and the other used to go about with tale-bearing."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for a branch, broke it into two pieces, and placed one piece on each of their graves. He was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Why did you do this? He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""It is hoped that their punishment will be lessened as long as these do not dry."""
"165","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to relieve himself, I would bring water for him and he would cleanse himself with that water."
"166","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): A Bedouin stood up and began to urinate in the mosque. The people wanted to attack him (i.e., beat him), but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: ""Leave him alone and pour a bucket of water over his urine, for you have been sent to make things easy, not to make things difficult."""
"167","Narrated from Umm Qais bint Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with her) that she brought her young child, who did not eat food, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) seated the child in his lap, and the child urinated on his clothes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for water and sprinkled it over the spot, and did not wash it."
"168","Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came near a place where a people used to throw their garbage, and (there) he stood and urinated. Then he asked for water, so I brought water to him, and he performed ablution."
"169","In one narration, it is reported from Hudhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him) that (when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, once urinated behind a wall), I moved away from him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, signaled to me. Thus, I went to him and stood behind him (that is, behind his back) until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, finished (urinating)."
"170","Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""Tell me, if one of us gets menstrual blood on her clothes, what should she do?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""She should scrape it off, then rub it with water, and then wash it with (more) water, and then she may pray in it."""
"171","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I am a woman who suffers from continuous bleeding (istihada) and therefore do not become pure for many days. Should I stop offering prayers?” The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, “No! This is blood from a vein and not menstruation. So when your menstrual period comes, stop offering prayers, and when it passes, wash the blood from your body and then offer prayers. Then perform ablution for every prayer until the (menstrual) period returns (then stop offering prayers again).”"
"172","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I used to wash the traces of janabah (semen stains) from the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out for prayer wearing the same garment, even though there would be water spots on his garment."
"173","‘Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that some people from (the tribe of) ‘Ukl or ‘Uraynah came, and the climate of Madinah did not suit them, so they became ill in Madinah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they be given some camels and also ordered that they drink their urine and milk. So they went (to the pasture) and did so. When they recovered, they killed the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shepherd and drove away the animals. Early in the day, this news reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent men in their pursuit. By mid-morning, they were brought (arrested). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that their hands and feet be cut off, and hot iron rods were passed over their eyes, and they were thrown on the hot stony ground. They would ask for water, but they were not given water (because they too had shown ingratitude)."
"174","`Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates,` Before the mosque was built, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to offer prayers in a sheepfold."
"175","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Allah’s Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about a mouse that had fallen into clarified butter (ghee). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Remove it and also remove the (ghee) around where it fell, and use the rest of the ghee.”"
"176","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Any wound that a Muslim receives in the way of Allah will appear on the Day of Resurrection in the same (fresh) state as it was when it was inflicted; blood will flow from it. Its color will be that of blood, but its fragrance will be that of musk."""
"177","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""None of you should urinate in standing water that does not flow, (because it is possible that) he may need to wash (himself) in that (water) again."""
"178","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him): The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying near the Ka’bah, and Abu Jahl and some of his friends were sitting there. One of them said to another, “Who among you will bring the entrails (and intestines, etc.) of such-and-such tribe’s she-camel and place it on Muhammad’s (peace be upon him) back when he goes into prostration?” So the most wretched among them (‘Uqbah) got up, brought it, and waited until the Prophet (peace be upon him) went into prostration. (Immediately) he placed it between the Prophet’s (peace be upon him) shoulders, and I was watching this state but could do nothing. If only I had the power (why would I have witnessed this state)! Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Then those people started laughing and fell over each other (out of laughter and joy), and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was in prostration and could not raise his head until Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) came and removed it from the Prophet’s (peace be upon him) back. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) raised his blessed head and supplicated against them, saying, “O Allah! Make destruction obligatory upon Quraysh.” He said this three times. This was very hard on them, because the Prophet (peace be upon him) had supplicated against them. Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Those disbelievers knew that supplication is accepted in this city (Makkah). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) mentioned each one by name: “O Allah! Make (the destruction of) Abu Jahl obligatory upon Yourself, and ‘Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, and Walid bin ‘Utbah, and Umayyah bin Khalaf, and ‘Uqbah bin Abi Mu’it (obligatory upon Yourself).” (And he counted a seventh, but I do not remember his name.) By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I saw those people whom the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had named, lying (dead and unburied) in the well, that is, the well of Badr."
"179","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his garment (once)."
"180","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that people asked him with what was the wound of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) treated. He replied that now there is no one left who knows more about it than me. (He then explained that) Amir al-Mu’minin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to bring water in his shield, and Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) used to wash the blood from the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then a mat was brought and burnt, and (the ashes) were filled into the wound of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"181","Narrated Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him): I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw that he was using a miswak in his hand and cleaning his teeth, and he was saying ""Aa, Aa,"" and the miswak was in his mouth as if he was about to vomit."
"182","Narrated Hudhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him): When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up at night, he would rub (clean) his mouth (teeth) with a miswak."
"183","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw myself in a dream cleaning my teeth with a miswak. Then two persons came to me, one of whom was older than the other. I gave the miswak to the younger of them, but I was told, 'Give it to the older one.' So I gave the miswak to the older of them."""
"184","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: “When you go to your bed, perform ablution as you do for prayer. Then lie down on your right side and then say: ‘O Allah! I have submitted my face to You, and entrusted my affairs to You, and I have taken You as my Protector and Refuge, hoping for You and fearing You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except with You. O Allah! I believe in Your Book which You have revealed and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.’ If you die that night, you will die upon faith. And say these words after you have said whatever else you wish to say (i.e., do not say anything after this).” Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I repeated these words before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I reached ‘I believe in Your Book which You have revealed,’ I said, ‘and Your Messenger.’ He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ‘No, but say: and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.’"
